{"timestamp": 1779431750.5141726, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 9, "data": {"caller": "player_5", "reason": "Frank reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "medbay", "victim_name": "Alice"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779431750.5151026, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 9, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779431760.8116229, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 9, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I just found Alice's body in medbay. Here's what I saw: earlier, around tick 4, Alice and Bob were both in medbay. I left and went to electrical, where I actually saw Bob again at tick 7. When I went back to medbay, Alice was dead. Bob, you were the last person I saw with Alice before I left medbay. What happened after I walked out, and when did you leave her? Everyone else, where were you?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779431769.0379517, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 9, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I started my tasks up in oxygen and then moved down to upper engine. To be honest, I haven't seen a single person this entire round, so I don't have an alibi and I can't vouch for anyone else. I was completely alone on the left side of the map. \n\nFrank's timeline sounds pretty specific, though. Bob, we definitely need to hear your side of the story \u2014 when did you leave medbay, and was Alice still alive when you left? Let's hear from Bob and the rest of the group before making any decisions."}}
{"timestamp": 1779431778.380621, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 9, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I started off in weapons, then moved down to security and navigation. I can vouch for Eve \u2014 I saw her in security around tick 3, and then we were both in navigation around ticks 7 and 8. We were on the complete opposite side of the map from medbay. \n\nWith Charlie on the left side, and Eve and me on the right, that leaves Frank and Bob in the middle near medbay. Frank, your timeline is very detailed, which makes Bob look incredibly suspicious. Bob, you really need to explain what happened in medbay. I'm leaning toward voting Bob unless he has a really good defense, but I want to hear from him and Eve first."}}
{"timestamp": 1779431792.0331628, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 9, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Diana is completely right. I was in security early on, and then I headed down to navigation. I saw Diana come into navigation around tick 7, and we've been together ever since. Since we were on the far right side of the ship the whole time, neither of us could have reached medbay to kill Alice. \n\nCharlie's on the far left, which means the kill almost certainly happened exactly how Frank described it in the middle of the map. Frank, your timeline is very precise, and it puts Bob squarely at the scene of the crime with the victim before moving to electrical. \n\nBob, you're up next, and you are the prime suspect right now. You need to explain exactly when you left Alice in medbay and where you went. Unless Bob has a bulletproof explanation or someone else saw him far away from medbay when the kill happened, I think Bob is our best vote today."}}
{"timestamp": 1779432786.2880425, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 9, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": ""}}
{"timestamp": 1779432809.0432487, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 9, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Like I said, the timeline is undeniable. Bob was the last person in medbay with Alice around tick 4. I bumped into him in electrical at tick 7, and when I went back to medbay, Alice was dead. Diana and Eve are clearing each other on the right side, and Charlie was on the far left. Bob is the only one who had the opportunity, and he doesn't seem to have any defense. I'm voting for Bob."}}
{"timestamp": 1779432828.1655173, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 9, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Bob, you didn't even defend yourself. Frank's timeline makes perfect sense, and with Diana and Eve clearing each other on the right side of the ship, you're the only one left who could have killed Alice in medbay. Everything points to you. I'm voting for Bob."}}
{"timestamp": 1779432838.1723192, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 9, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Bob"}}
{"timestamp": 1779432854.1781092, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 9, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Since Bob has completely stayed silent and offered absolutely no defense against Frank's detailed timeline, the choice here is obvious. Diana and I have been together on the right side, and Charlie was on the far left, leaving Bob as the only possible culprit. I'm voting for Bob."}}
{"timestamp": 1779432885.9612927, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 9, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I\u2019m not silent \u2014 I was trying to get the timeline straight. I started storage, went medbay, and yes, I saw Alice there with Frank. I did not kill her. Alice was alive when I left medbay and I went to electrical, where Frank also saw me at tick 7. After that I went to security, which is where I was when the report happened.\n\nFrank is leaving out that he was also in medbay with Alice early, then he\u2019s the one who went back and \u201cfound\u201d the body. If I killed Alice in medbay, why would I then run to electrical where Frank sees me and then end up all the way in security instead of hiding? The only person who went back to medbay alone and reported is Frank.\n\nI think this is a self-report or at least Frank pushing way too hard off \u201clast seen\u201d when he had just as much access to that room. I\u2019m voting Frank."}}
